      {
        "id": 26071,
        "name": "arenson9",
        "username": "arenson9",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/arenson9/{size}/1900_2.png",
        "created_at": "2012-04-20T13:09:25.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Two more great events yesterday. We weren’t sure we’d have anyone at all at Downtown Comics in the middle of the day, but we had some regulars drop by AND a handful of new players. It was great. Then, at Arsenal, things were really hopping – three tables playing simultaneously with more people waiting for their turn. Also, for those of you who don’t follow Christopher’s Tweets (<span class=\"mention\">@SentinelsOfTheMultiverse</span>), we had both myself (The Deputy) and one of the Enforcers, so Chris shared a pic of us holding our cards.</p>\n<p>Normally for game days and demos we’ll play abbreviated games using the simpler-to-play heroes, but one of the games we played last night was five players versus a fully HP’d Spite. Took a loooong time, but was an epic win: Four of five heroes were incapacitated and Mr. Fixer was down to 3 HP when Expatriette finished off Spite with one of her Incapacitated abilities.</p>",
        "post_number": 22,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:59:59.918Z",
